* ========================================================================================================
* Gyrator–Capacitor (GC) subcircuit for saturable, hysteretic cores
* Inputs: 
*   N1 – “flux” node (one side of magnetic capacitance)
*   N2 – the other side of the magnetic capacitance
*   N4 – node at which the nonlinear hysteretic branch returns
* Params: 
*   C  = magnetizing capacitance
*   a,n = parameters for “saturation” nonlinearity
*   R   = resistor in the hysteresis branch
*   b,m = parameters for the hysteresis nonlinearity
* ========================================================================================================
.SUBCKT CORE_GC N1 N2 N4 PARAMS: C=1e-3 a=1 n=2 R=1 b=1 m=1
  * Magnetic Capacitance representing the permeance (and saturation)
  Cc N1 N2 {C}

  * Nonlinear “saturation” controlled source – note use of AUX functions.
  Bc N2 N3 V = {a} * (ABS(V(N1,N2)))**{n} * SGN(V(N1,N2))

  * Hysteresis branch (a resistor in series with a nonlinear source)
  Rr N3 N4 {R}
  Br N3 N4 I = {b} * (ABS(V(N3,N4)))**{m} * SGN(V(N3,N4))
.ENDS CORE_GC

