* Single–Ended Transformer Model
* Primary ports: P1, P2; Secondary ports: S1, S2
* The transformer is modeled by:
*   – A gyrator (voltage–controlled source) that converts the time–derivative of 
*     the magnetic “flux” (the voltage across the magnetizing capacitor) into a 
*     winding voltage.
*   – A nonlinear GC block that models core saturation and hysteresis.
* ========================================================================================================
.SUBCKT SingleEnded P1 P2 S1 S2 PARAMS: C=1e-3 a=1 n=2 R=1 b=1 m=1 Np=100 Ns=50
  Vp P1 C2 0

  * Primary winding: The induced voltage is proportional to the derivative of the flux.
  * (Note the negative sign – see below for push–pull where polarity is adjusted.)
  * Exact realization: I(L) = I(Vp), V(L) = Np*dI/dt.
  Fddt_p 0 ddt_p Vp 1
  Lddt_p ddt_p 0 {Np}
  Bp P1 C1 V = V(ddt_p)
  * Instance of the GC (magnetic core) block.
  XGC C1 C2 P2 CORE_GC PARAMS: C={C} a={a} n={n} R={R} b={b} m={m}

  * Secondary winding: The induced voltage on the secondary is proportional to the flux derivative.
  Bs S1 S2 V = {Ns} * I(Bp)
.ENDS SingleEnded

* ========================================================================================================
* Push–Pull Transformer Model
* Primary ports: P1, P2 (each half–winding), Center Tap: CT; Secondary ports: S1, S2
* In a push–pull design the two primary halves are driven in anti–phase.
* ========================================================================================================
.SUBCKT PushPull P1 CT P2 S1 S2 PARAMS: C=1e-3 a=1 n=2 R=1 b=1 m=1 Np=100 Ns=50
  .PARAM Np2 = {Np/2}

  Vp1 P1 C3 0
  Vp2 C4 P2 0

  * Primary winding halves: each half provides half the total turns.
  * Exact realization: I(L) = I(Vp1), V(L) = Np2*dI/dt.
  Fddt_p1 0 ddt_p1 Vp1 1
  Lddt_p1 ddt_p1 0 {Np2}
  Bp1 P1 C1 V = V(ddt_p1)
  * Exact realization: I(L) = I(Vp2), V(L) = Np2*dI/dt.
  Fddt_p2 0 ddt_p2 Vp2 1
  Lddt_p2 ddt_p2 0 {Np2}
  Bp2 C2 P2 V = V(ddt_p2)
  * Two GC blocks model the two halves of the core.
  XGC1 C1 C3 CT CORE_GC PARAMS: C={C} a={a} n={n} R={R} b={b} m={m}
  XGC2 C2 C4 CT CORE_GC PARAMS: C={C} a={a} n={n} R={R} b={b} m={m}

  Bs S1 S2 V = {Ns} * (I(Bp1) + I(Bp2))/2
.ENDS PushPull

